00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.320
Jack: One of the ways to communicate
effectively is to tailor the

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.859
communication to the audience.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.340
If done correctly it should result in
engaging the audience with good results.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.939
In business communication will involve
people at different levels of ability and

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.209
understanding, some may be colleagues who
understand what is being communicated,

00:00:18.719 --> 00:00:22.836
some may be customers who might not be
fully conversant and need to be informed.

00:00:22.836 --> 00:00:26.360
There are also different channels of
communication that must be considered

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.160
when communicating to different
audiences, from giving out information

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.949
generally, via social media or contacting
individuals directly via email.

00:00:35.799 --> 00:00:39.640
Leah: Adapting communication style can
depend on whether the communication and

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.170
interaction is face to face or digital.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.100
In person communication gives
the opportunity to observe body

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.819
language and can help in deciding
if a change of tone is needed.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.209
The tone should also suit the audience,
respecting their views and not

00:00:54.209 --> 00:00:56.110
being too preachy or condescending.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.230
Over email or digital communication,
the message should be more

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:03.690
considered to be able to put it
across clearly and concisely.

00:01:04.219 --> 00:01:08.060
Jack: Working with a team and presenting
ideas face to face, will give opportunity

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.859
for interaction and active listening
and the opportunity for feedback,

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:13.649
questioning and further discussion.

00:01:14.879 --> 00:01:17.710
Vocabulary used should always fit
the audience the communication

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.780
is aimed at, and any complex
elements should be explained in

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.510
a way that others can understand.

